<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n84421" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολεμ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for war,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ π. κίνδυνοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.43
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγῶνες π.,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρηνικοί,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				729d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				829a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλοῖα, ὅπλα,</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				706b
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				944e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκῆν ἀσπίδα -ωτάτην εἶναι</span>”
				<i>most fit for service,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Lac.</u>
					11.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρεία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>OGI</u>
					54.13
				</span></i>
			 (Egypt, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη καὶ ἐπιστήμη π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					522c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				639b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ -κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>) <i>the art of war,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Sph.</u>
				222c
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ -κά</span>
			<i>warlike exercises,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ π ἄλκιμος</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολέμια</span>
			) <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ π. ἀσκεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					3.4.18
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				1.5.9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ τῶν π. μελέται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.39
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				89
			</span></i> (v.l.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -κόν</span>
			<i>signal for battle</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιὼν
			π.</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				348b
			</span></i>), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπειδὰν ὁ σαλπικτὴς σημήνῃ</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					4.3.29
				</span></i>
			, cf. Aen. Tact.<i><span class="en">
				4.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνέκραγε πολεμικόν</span> gave
			a <i>war</i>-shout, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				7.3.33
			</span></i>; also of <i>an air on the flute,</i> Tryphoap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				14.618c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>fighting part</i> of the people, opp. civilians, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1291a26
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1329a2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<i>skilled in war, warlike,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.84
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				522e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				643c
			</span></i>, etc.: distd. from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλοπόλεμος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				2.6.1
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵπποι π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					7.5.62
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ π.</span>”
				<i>warlike spirit,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Mus.</u>
					p.27
				</span></i>
			 K. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>like an enemy, hostile,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Vect.</u>
				4.44
			</span></i>; <i>stirring up hostility,</i> opp. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλικός, πολεμικὸν ἔρις καὶ ὀργή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					2.6.21
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίθεσις π. καὶ ἀσύμβατος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.946e
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς, ἔχειν,</span> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰρηνικῶς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				5.46
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. διακεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					6.39
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτατα, ἔχειν πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>An.</u>
					6.1.1
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
